 17592186045417 true] [17592186446148 1074 "Note that $A$ is not aligned with the zero-mark on the ruler. \n\nTo find the length, we read the values that correspond to the points $A$ and $B,$ and take the difference.\n\nFrom the picture, we deduce that $A$ corresponds to $2\\,\\text{in}$ while $B$ corresponds to $3.5\\,\\text{in}.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB=3.5\\,\\text{in}-2\\,\\text{in}=1.5\\,\\text{in}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534970 17592186045417 true] [17592186446149 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446139 13194139534970 17592186045417 true] [17592186446149 1069 "q-113157" 13194139534970 17592186045417 true] [17592186446149 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534970 17592186045417 true] [17592186446149 1071 "![](images/2f/2f148af3e47726793c57ad48ab608d90fb8378da4651973c2ba864f54633e2b4.png)\n\nWhat is the measure of the line segment $\\overset{―}{MN}$ shown above?" 13194139534970 17592186045417 true] [17592186446149 1072 #uuid "2b5924f6-1b4f-5cd0-89f3-79b22bdc59d5" 13194139534970 17592186045417 true] [17592186446149 1074 "Note that the length of a side of one cell is \n\n$$\n\\frac{1\\,\\text{in}}{4}=0.25\\,\\text{in}.\n$$\n\nThe line segment has a length of $7$ cells, hence the total measure is \n\n$$\nMN=7\\cdot 0.25\\,\\text{in}=1.75\\,\\text{in}.\n$$" 13194139534970 17592186045417 true] [17592186446150 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446142 13194139534970 17592186045417 true] [17592186446150 1069 "q-52868" 13194139534970 17592186045417 true] [17592186446150 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534970 17592186045417 true] [17592186446150 1071 "![](images/53/5349fd8cce4fc4c31f4ddf54616158cc9bc1755b78011bdbc699fd5253524382.png)\n\nFind the length of the line segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ shown above." 13194139534970 17592186045417 true] [17592186446150 1072 #uuid "41aa9532-ccbf-54f2-a095-f66029205574" 13194139534970 17592186045417 true] [17592186446150 1074 "To find the length, we read the values that correspond to the points $A$ and $B$ and take the difference.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that $A$ corresponds to $-4$ units while $B$ corresponds to $1$ units.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\nAB=1-(-4)=5\\,\\text{units}.\n$$" 13194139534970 17592186045417 true] [17592186446151 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446146 13194139534970 17592186045417 true] [17592186446151 1069 "q-20579" 13194139534970 17592186045417 true] [17592186446151 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534970 17592186045417 true] [17592186446151 1071 "![](images/ba/ba75204629bffa2aea805fa09cd3b5bd01c24f28edd7ba7d154b93fa9b16e5a0.png)\n\nFor the figure shown above, how many line segments are there?" 13194139534970 17592186045417 true] [17592186446151 1072 #uuid "718c9427-3023-5517-97ab-03ae81fa561f" 13194139534970 17592186045417 true] [17592186446151 1074 "From the diagram, we can count $6$ line segments:\n$\\overset{―}{PQ}$ , $\\overset{―}{PR}$, $\\overset{―}{PS}$ , $\\overset{―}{QR}$ , $\\overset{―}{QS}$, $\\overset{―}{RS}.$" 13194139534970 17592186045417 true] [17592186446152 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446144 13194139534970 17592186045417 true] [17592186446152 1069 "q-53112" 13194139534970 17592186045417 true] [17592186446152 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534970 17592186045417 true] [17592186446152 1071 "![](images/03/033a552ea0d8d76033a8701e4cfe5cbbb8009f18a9329406722e70e498310448.png)\n\nFind the length of the line segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ shown above." 13194139534970 17592186045417 true] [17592186446152 1072 #uuid "751ce1db-dc08-51e0-8ae8-024841607cc5" 13194139534970 17592186045417 true] [17592186446152 1074 "To find the length, we read the values that correspond to the points $A$ and $B$ and take the difference.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that $A$ corresponds to $-12$ units while $B$ corresponds to $-5$ units.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\nAB=-5-(-12)=7\\,\\text{units}.\n$$" 13194139534970 17592186045417 true] [17592186446153 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446140 13194139534970 17592186045417 true] [17592186446153 1069 "q-67642" 13194139534970 17592186045417 true] [17592186446153 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534970 17592186045417 true] [17592186446153 1071 "![](images/d6/d67e2cb1a53f6063cf798294cbf077729bb3cf3621ba242325129b81dfe6c791.png)\n\nWhat is the measure of the line segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ shown above?" 13194139534970 17592186045417 true] [17592186446153 1072 #uuid "b6e9a199-9ae7-5749-8e50-9bec321630b9" 13194139534970 17592186045417 true] [17592186446153 1074 "Note that the length of a side of one cell is \n\n$$\n\\frac{6\\,\\text{m}}{3}=2\\,\\text{m}.\n$$\n\nThe line segment has a length of $6$ cells, hence the total measure is \n\n$$\nAB=6\\cdot 2\\,\\text{m}=12\\,\\text{m}.\n$$" 13194139534970 17592186045417 true] [17592186446154 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446145 13194139534970 17592186045417 true] [17592186446154 1069 "q-53228" 13194139534970 17592186045417 true] [17592186446154 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534970 17592186045417 true] [17592186446154 1071 "Which of the following pictures shows a line segment of $7.5\\,\\text{cm}$ long?" 13194139534970 17592186045417 true] [17592186446154 1072 #uuid "f3042f6b-9d86-5ac2-aea7-7fc852598853" 13194139534970 17592186045417 true] [17592186446154 1074 "Note that one of the points of each segment is aligned with the zero-mark on the ruler.\n\nWe will use the rulers to determine which segment has a length of $7.5\\,\\text{cm}.$ To do this, we need to find a picture where the value that corresponds to the second point gives us exactly $7.5.$\n\nThe correct option is the following.\n\n![](images/39/392b3af6a2e540510c8bb19350226faebe2d2a6183da015473ba5379a8a92d5d.png)" 13194139534970 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-0116267a-587a-59de-84d1-6ba467b65702" 17592186446094 "answer-03170d95-31f2-5da2-aa85-7c107c5b9773" 17592186446095 "answer-05b96e9a-3e82-5e77-b97f-219a5a16bbad" 17592186446096 "answer-0c9e393a-c83f-56e2-abff-a9c32c985ab0" 17592186446097 "answer-0f3613bc-9742-5631-8d02-060c3a922a0e" 17592186446098 "answer-126a485c-1c8c-5e8c-9aae-240